<title>USA: U.S. top 20 best selling vehicles in 1996.</title>
<headline>U.S. top 20 best selling vehicles in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following chart represents the 20 most popular cars and light trucks in the United States, based on full-year 1996 sales results reported by major automakers.</p>
<p>MAKE/MODEL			1996 SALES  1995 SALES  1995 RANK</p>
<p> 1. Ford F-Series Pickup	 780,838   691,452	  1.</p>
<p> 2. Chevrolet C-K Pickup	 526,960   513,081	  2.</p>
<p> 3. Ford Explorer		  402,663   395,227	  3.</p>
<p> 4. Ford Taurus		    401,049   366,266	  4.</p>
<p> 5. Dodge Ram Pickup	     383,960   271,501	 11.</p>
<p> 6. Honda Accord		   382,298   341,384	  5.</p>
<p> 7. Toyota Camry		   359,433   328,600	  6.</p>
<p> 8. Dodge Caravan		  300,117   264,937	 12.</p>
<p> 9. Ford Ranger Pickup	   288,393   309,085	  7.</p>
<p>10. Honda Civic/Del Sol	  286,350   289,435	  8.</p>
<p>11. Ford Escort		    284,644   285,570	 10.</p>
<p>12. Jeep Grand Cherokee	  279,195   252,186	 13.</p>
<p>13. Saturn			   278,574   285,674	  9.</p>
<p>14. Chevrolet Cavalier	   277,222   212,767	 19.</p>
<p>15. Chevrolet Blazer	     246,307   214,661	 16.</p>
<p>16. Chevrolet Lumina	     237,973   214,595	 17.</p>
<p>17. Pontiac Grand Am	     222,477   234,226	 14.</p>
<p>18. Toyota Corolla		 209,048   213,640	 18.</p>
<p>19. Ford Windstar		  209,033   222,147	 15.</p>
<p>20. Chevrolet S-10 Pickup	190,178   207,193	 20.</p>
</text>
